From 419318be775f8b6c2659467f39c9595eab734dbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmed Adel Wafdy <fandes99@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:20:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Cargo.lock

Yocto's cargo class fetches crates from the lock file, which the
repository does not carry. Generated with cargo generate-lockfile,
resolved for Rust 1.75 (scarthgap), with ignore and globset held at
the last releases before edition 2024, and written as lock file
version 3, the newest cargo 1.75 reads (crates.io sources only, so
versions 3 and 4 are the same otherwise).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [no Cargo.lock upstream; local build pinning]
Signed-off-by: Ahmed Adel Wafdy <fandes99@gmail.com>
---
 Cargo.lock | 1051 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 1051 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Cargo.lock

diff --git a/Cargo.lock b/Cargo.lock
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..584bec5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Cargo.lock
@@ -0,0 +1,1051 @@
